hat determines what business it can run, and once you give them a plot and a house they work largely on their own, managing stock, setting aside produce for taxes and trading with others.\n\nBecause villagers buy and sell in a free market, supply and demand drive what goods are worth. You can also hold events and conduct diplomacy. Lords and Villeins is a single-player simulation that suits players who enjoy economic depth and watching systems interact."}}